       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Higher doses carry more risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects, and they haven't been shown to work better. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that ceiling.\n\nPlease check which of these applies:\n\n1. **Dose typo.** If you meant 40 mg or 200 mg, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. Typical dosing is 50 mg daily to start, titrated up to a maximum of 200 mg daily.\n2. **Deliberate off-label dosing.** If you mean to go above the maximum, for example on a psychiatry recommendation, tell me that's intentional. I can enter it with a note recording the rationale, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n3. **Different drug or formulation.** If you meant another medication, let me know."
